{"title":"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two of the three sides of a triangle are 20 and 15. Which of the following numbers is not a possible perimeter of the triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a731032c53ae3862252152289d1224277b31c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 52\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 57\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 62\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 67\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the third side, then by the triangle inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a10c432509ff670fe7ff0a22770da585fbb483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-15 &lt; x &lt; 20+15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/7181fcbb3665195a9c6f509a6f59b59fcebc49fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 &lt; x &lt; 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore the perimeter must be greater than 40 but less than 70. 72 is not in this range, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d5e714b804d77b9aa7e45c16fbe405ae72e76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\, 72}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" /> is our answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A\">2015 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=